{"availability":"available","full":"poulpy-fhe/poulpy","name":"poulpy","description":"A backend agnostic modular FHE library over the Torus using bivariate polynomial representation","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":87,"forks":18,"created":"2024-12-04T09:53:09Z","updated":"2026-10-07T21:05:01Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://squid.cedoor.dev/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:11.231Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:11.231Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:11.231Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T04:52:11.231Z","stars":87,"forks":18}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["📖 poulpy.dev: quickstart, architecture, layouts, benchmarks, ecosystem and the documentation for CKKS, binary FHE, security and the API.","Poulpy is a fast and modular FHE library that implements Ring-Learning-With-Errors based homomorphic encryption over the Torus. It adopts the bivariate polynomial representation proposed in Revisiting Key Decomposition Techniques for FHE: Simpler, Faster and More Generic to represent Torus polynomials. Compared with the residue number system (RNS), this representation provides simpler and more reusable arithmetic, a common plaintext space for all schemes, and native bridges between schemes. Poulpy also decouples scheme implementations from the polynomial arithmetic backend by being built from…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/poulpy-fhe/poulpy/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"247e45503529b822bc7329b65ce26ec75ab4b741010b85ebaf510c0b0c322a67","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:11.312Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:11.312Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"📖 poulpy.dev: quickstart, architecture, layouts, benchmarks, ecosystem and the documentation for CKKS, binary FHE, security and the API.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/poulpy-fhe/poulpy/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requi